set_note(address=CODE:0x0..0x1, note=Note(content=r#"VT510 firmware 23-032ED-00: a 512KB ROM holding eight 64KB banks, mapped into one 19-bit CODE space: bank N sits at CODE:0xN0000. P1.7 = A16, P1.6 = A17, P1.5 = A18 select the bank (the VT520 uses P1.4-P1.6 with P1.4 low); all 1038 self-stubs land on a matching slot with this order and only 582 with P1.6/P1.7 swapped.
Cross-bank calls use trampoline slots (0x0E70-0x1CE4 in each bank): bit ops that change the bank, LCALL, bit ops that restore it, RET. A slot whose LCALL targets itself is an outgoing stub (bN_far_<target>); the new bank's slot at the same offset is the landing (bN_land_<target>) and calls the real routine.
Banks 0-3 reset to 0x0E70 (SETB P1.5 -> bank 4). Banks 4-7 reset to their own entry, the target of the slot at 0x0E72: bank 4 0x1140, 5 0x13A4, 6 0x1434, 7 0x17F0. Bank 4's 0x1140 sets P1.6 and P1.7 -> bank 7, whose entry 0x17F0 matches the VT525's bank 7 0x2947. ROM ID "DEC510" at 0x2A (AA 55 marker at 0x26)."#, fields={}, id="00000000000000000000000000", links=[], tags=["banking"]))
